# Presence of this file enables the SD-card swap tier (/dev/mmcblk0p4) in
# /etc/init.d/S02swap. Delete it and reboot to run on zram alone -- the card is
# then never written for swap at all.
#
# It is shipped present because the SD backstop was asked for, but note that in
# normal operation it should stay at 0 kB used: zram (priority 100) must fill
# its 16 MiB mem_limit before the kernel touches this (priority 10). A non-zero
# Used column for mmcblk0p4 in /proc/swaps is a bug report, not routine.
#
#   awk '$1=="/dev/mmcblk0p4" {print "SD swap used:", $4, "kB"}' /proc/swaps
#
# S02swap logs /proc/swaps and the p4 block write counter to /var/log/swap.log
# on every shutdown so the wear trail is visible.
